  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16:\n\n> Bug; Lead in / Lead out - Helix Pitch, Auto cannot relaly be turned off. As soon as i try to change the input it will switch back to auto on its own - same ggoes for the \"other\" auto calculated inputs.\n\nWhat happens:\n\n- The user opens the Lead in / Lead out group of an operation.\n- The user turns off `Auto` on `Helix pitch` and starts to type a value.\n- The input switches back to `Auto` during the edit. The typed value is lost.\n- The other inputs that have an `Auto` toggle do the same.\n\nExpected:\n\n- `Auto` stays off until the user turns it on again.\n- The typed value is kept, goes through the command history (`EditOperationParams`), and one undo step restores the earlier state.\n- The generator and the posted program use the typed value.\n\nPoints to check in the work:\n\n- Find what sets `Auto` again: a compare of the typed value with the computed value on each frame, an edit command for each key press that writes the computed value back, or a rule that reads an empty or equal value as `Auto`.\n- Check each parameter that has an `Auto` toggle, on each operation page, not only `Helix pitch`. List them in the PR.\n- Check that a value saved as manual stays manual after save and reopen.\n- Check the same parameters through MCP: a manual value set there must stay manual.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A UI test pins that, with `Auto` off, typed digits stay in the `Helix pitch` input and `Auto` stays off, across several frames.\n- A test covers each other parameter with an `Auto` toggle, or one test that goes through the shared widget and the list of its users.\n- A test pins that the manual value reaches the operation parameters and that undo restores `Auto`.\n",
